$$SYNTAX-LEVEL 2
*(mgdb-alphafill
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary">
<meta name="twitter:site" content="@MaizeGDB">
<meta property="og:url" content="https\://maizegdb.org/data_center/alphafill">
<meta property="og:title" content="MaizeGDB AlphaFill | Predicted Ligands, Cofactors &amp; Metal Sites">
<meta property="og:description" content="Explore AlphaFill ligand hypotheses for B73 RefGen_v5 proteins, inspect predicted binding sites in 3D, and download the complete dataset.">

<a class="mgdb-skip-link" href="#af-main">Skip to main content</a>
<main class="mgdb-page mgdb-alphafill-page" id="af-main">

  <nav class="mgdb-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span><a href="/sitemap">Data hubs</a><span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span><a href="/data_center/protein_structure">Protein Structures</a><span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span><span aria-current="page">AlphaFill</span>
  </nav>

  <section class="mgdb-hero" aria-labelledby="af-title">
    <div class="mgdb-hero-emblem">
      <img src="/images/data_center/protein_structure.png?v=20260822" alt="Protein structure icon" class="af-hero-icon" width="80" height="80" />
      <strong>Ligand<br />Transplants</strong>
    </div>
    <div class="mgdb-hero-body">
      <p class="mgdb-hero-stamp"><span aria-hidden="true">&#9679;</span> AlphaFill $(af-version) &middot; PDB-REDO $(databank-date) &middot; Indexed $(data-date)</p>
      <h1 id="af-title">What might this maize protein bind?</h1>
      <p class="mgdb-hero-description">Search a B73 RefGen_v5 gene or protein to inspect ligands transferred from similar experimental structures. Select a result to focus the predicted site in 3D, compare confidence, and follow its donor evidence.</p>
      <p class="mgdb-hero-actions">
        <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-primary" href="#af-gene">Search a gene</a>
        <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary" href="/data_center/alphafill/faq">How to interpret results</a>
        <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-quiet" href="/data_center/protein_structure">Protein structure hub <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <aside class="af-intro" aria-label="What AlphaFill results mean">
    <div>
      <strong>Every row is a hypothesis.</strong>
      <span>A transplant is a ligand copied from a related PDB structure after its local binding site is aligned to the maize model. It is a prediction, not an observation in maize and not a docking result.</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <strong>Ligand is a broad term.</strong>
      <span>Results include cofactors, metabolites, drugs, metal ions, small molecules, peptides and proteins. Crystallization additives and likely adventitious ions are retained but clearly flagged.</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <strong>No donor does not mean no ligand.</strong>
      <span>If no PDB homolog clears AlphaFill's 25% identity floor, the result reports a coverage gap rather than claiming that the protein binds nothing.</span>
    </div>
  </aside>

  <nav class="mgdb-section-tabs" aria-label="AlphaFill sections">
    <a href="#af-gene" class="is-current" aria-current="location">Gene lookup</a>
    <a href="#af-ligand">Ligand lookup</a>
    <a href="#af-downloads">Downloads</a>
    <a href="/data_center/alphafill/faq">FAQ &amp; methods</a>
  </nav>

  <section class="mgdb-panel af-workspace marker-search-panel" id="af-gene" aria-labelledby="af-gene-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading af-heading-stacked">
      <div><h2 id="af-gene-title">Find the predicted ligands for a gene</h2></div>
    </div>
    <p class="af-section-intro">Accepts B73 RefGen_v5 gene models, protein isoforms, and older identifiers, locus names and gene symbols that resolve to one. Ligand codes and chemical names work here too and open the ligand view.</p>

    <form class="af-search" id="af-search-form" autocomplete="off" role="search">
      <label class="mgdb-label" for="af-search-input">Gene model, protein isoform, or ligand</label>
      <div class="af-search-row">
        <div class="af-search-field">
          <input class="mgdb-input af-search-input" id="af-search-input" type="search" name="term"
                 role="combobox" aria-autocomplete="list" aria-expanded="false"
                 aria-controls="af-suggestions" aria-describedby="af-search-hint"
                 placeholder="Zm00001eb086870, 086870, NAD, flavin&hellip;" />
          <div class="mgdb-suggestions af-suggestions" id="af-suggestions" role="listbox"
               aria-label="Matching genes and ligands" hidden></div>
        </div>
        <button class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-primary af-search-submit" type="submit">Show ligands</button>
      </div>
      <p class="mgdb-hint" id="af-search-hint">Type at least two characters. A gene's numeric tail works on its own &mdash; <code>086870</code> finds <code>Zm00001eb086870</code>.</p>
      <div class="marker-example-row af-examples" aria-label="Example gene searches">
        <span>Example genes</span>
        <button class="mgdb-chip" type="button" data-af-example="Zm00001eb086870" title="Strong transplant example">Zm00001eb086870</button>
        <button class="mgdb-chip" type="button" data-af-example="Zm00001eb000080" title="Multiple ligand example">Zm00001eb000080</button>
        <button class="mgdb-chip" type="button" data-af-example="Zm00001eb034000" title="Predicted pocket with no donor">Zm00001eb034000</button>
        <button class="mgdb-chip" type="button" data-af-example="Zm00001eb380210" title="Additive flags example">Zm00001eb380210</button>
      </div>
    </form>

    <noscript>
      <p class="mgdb-message mgdb-message-info">The ligand search and 3D viewer need JavaScript. The full dataset remains available in the downloads below.</p>
    </noscript>

    <div id="af-results" class="af-results" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="mgdb-empty af-welcome">
        <p><strong>Search a gene to see what it is predicted to bind.</strong></p>
        <p>The result combines the AlphaFold model, transplanted ligands, predicted P2Rank pockets, donor structures and confidence measures in one workspace.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mgdb-panel" id="af-ligand" aria-labelledby="af-ligand-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="af-ligand-title">Find maize genes by ligand</h2></div>
      <p>$(ligand-count) distinct PDB Chemical Component Dictionary entries occur in this run. Results are ranked by evidence and donor identity.</p>
    </div>

    <form class="af-search af-search-compact" id="af-ligand-form" autocomplete="off" role="search">
      <label class="mgdb-label" for="af-ligand-input">Ligand code or chemical name</label>
      <div class="af-search-row">
        <input class="mgdb-input" id="af-ligand-input" type="search" name="ccd"
               placeholder="NAD, FAD, ATP, HEM, SAM&hellip;" />
        <button class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary" type="submit">List genes</button>
      </div>
      <p class="mgdb-hint">Codes follow the <a href="https\://www.wwpdb.org/data/ccd" target="_blank" rel="noopener">wwPDB Chemical Component Dictionary</a>. Search accepts either a code such as <code>FAD</code> or a name such as <code>flavin</code>.</p>
      <div class="marker-example-row af-examples" aria-label="Example ligands">
        <span>Common cofactors</span>
        <button class="mgdb-chip" type="button" data-af-ligand="NAD">NAD</button>
        <button class="mgdb-chip" type="button" data-af-ligand="FAD">FAD</button>
        <button class="mgdb-chip" type="button" data-af-ligand="ATP">ATP</button>
        <button class="mgdb-chip" type="button" data-af-ligand="HEM">HEM</button>
        <button class="mgdb-chip" type="button" data-af-ligand="SAM">SAM</button>
        <button class="mgdb-chip" type="button" data-af-ligand="PLP">PLP</button>
      </div>
    </form>

    <div id="af-ligand-results" class="af-results" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="mgdb-empty"><p>Choose a ligand to list every maize gene that received it. Ions and additives remain searchable and are labelled by class.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="af-downloads" aria-labelledby="af-downloads-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="af-downloads-title">Download AlphaFill data</h2></div>
      <p>Use the compact gene tables for browsing and spreadsheets, or download the complete transplant record for reproducible analysis.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-card-grid af-download-grid">
      <article class="mgdb-card af-download-card">
        <span class="mgdb-pill mgdb-pill-info">JSON &middot; ~0.6 MB</span>
        <h3>Browse-ready gene index</h3>
        <p>One row for each of the $(genes-with) genes with a transplant: chromosome, model pLDDT, ligand counts, best evidence class and confident-pocket count.</p>
        <p class="af-card-action"><a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-quiet" href="/search/alphafill/alphafill_download.php?file=index">Download gene index <span aria-hidden="true">&darr;</span></a></p>
      </article>
      <article class="mgdb-card af-download-card">
        <span class="mgdb-pill mgdb-pill-warn">CSV &middot; ~3 MB</span>
        <h3>Predicted pockets with no donor</h3>
        <p>The $(target-count) well-modelled genes where P2Rank finds a confident pocket but AlphaFill finds no qualifying donor, with pLDDT and pocket probability.</p>
        <p class="af-card-action"><a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-quiet" href="/search/alphafill/alphafill_download.php?file=targets">Download target list <span aria-hidden="true">&darr;</span></a></p>
      </article>
      <article class="mgdb-card af-download-card">
        <span class="mgdb-pill mgdb-pill-info">JSON &middot; ~15 MB</span>
        <h3>Gene &times; ligand table</h3>
        <p>All $(pairs) distinct gene&ndash;ligand pairs with the best donor, identity, local RMSD, TCS, donor count and evidence class.</p>
        <p class="af-card-action"><a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-quiet" href="/search/alphafill/alphafill_download.php?file=by_gene">Download pair table <span aria-hidden="true">&darr;</span></a></p>
      </article>
      <article class="mgdb-card af-download-card">
        <span class="mgdb-pill">TSV.GZ &middot; ~64 MB</span>
        <h3>Every raw transplant</h3>
        <p>All $(transplants) transplants before collapsing, including donor PDB entry, ligand and donor CCD codes, identity, alignment, RMSD, clashes, TCS and ligand class.</p>
        <p class="af-card-action"><a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-quiet" href="/search/alphafill/alphafill_download.php?file=transplants">Download transplants <span aria-hidden="true">&darr;</span></a></p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <aside class="mgdb-note mgdb-note-info af-download-help">
      <p><strong>Need field definitions, corpus statistics or provenance?</strong> The <a href="/data_center/alphafill/faq">AlphaFill FAQ and methods page</a> documents each file, explains P2Rank, and describes the limits of these hypotheses.</p>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section id="af-resources" aria-labelledby="af-resources-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="af-resources-title">Related resources</h2></div>
      <p>Continue from a gene, structure or ligand without losing context.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mgdb-resource-panel">
      <div class="mgdb-resource-list">
        <a href="/data_center/protein_structure"><strong>Protein Structure Data Hub</strong><span>AlphaFold monomers, homodimers and heterodimers, with ESMFold isoform models</span></a>
        <a href="/projects/interpro_domain_atlas"><strong>InterPro Domain Atlas</strong><span>Check whether a predicted pocket falls inside a known functional domain</span></a>
        <a href="$(blast-url)"><strong>Sequence search</strong><span>No transplant for your protein? Find a close homolog that has one</span></a>
        <a href="https\://alphafill.science/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>AlphaFill databank</strong><span>The reference implementation and source databank</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>
)
